  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Education for Rohingya Refugee Children and Host Community Children in</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The 2nd phase of Education Cannot Wait (ECW) MYRP (2022-24) is built on the achievements of the previous MYRP (2018-2021) by continuing to directly meet the needs of adolescents and children in Cox&apos;s Bazar District in Bangladesh. The grantees of UN Consortium are UNESCO, UNHCR and UNICEF where UNICEF is the consortium lead agency. The focus of the MYRP is to improve access, quality, mental health and psychosocial support (MHPSS), disability inclusion, gender equity, continuity, child protection, mobilization of resources and improvements in the education system. UNESCO will contribute to OUTCOMES 1 (ACCESS), 2 (EQUITY AND INCLUSIVITY), 4 (SYSTEMS STRENGTHENING) and 5 (RESOURCE MOBILISATION).
The additional funding received from the donor for 2024 and 2025 will contribute to OUTCOME 3 (QUALITY) and OUTCOME 4 (STSTEMS STRENGTHENING).</narrative>
  </description>
